description:
Audit of the ants chat question and tool request interface against Claude Code's permission prompt and AskUserQuestion tool.

Today: ask_human question cards answer on 1-9 at once (crates/ants/src/tui/question.rs), but tool request cards need a, A or r then y (crates/ants/src/tui/approvals.rs, and ants dash), so each answer takes two keys. Claude Code's permission prompt commits on one key (1 Yes, 2 Yes and don't ask again for <rule>, 3 No and tell Claude what to do differently (esc)) and names what "don't ask again" covers; its AskUserQuestion takes 1-4 questions (header, options with label and description, multiSelect, an automatic Other row) answered with one submit.

Findings, one child each:
- the y confirmation step on tool requests;
- a key on a question card can answer a newer question than the one shown (Job::Answer carries only the thread);
- options on one line, typed answers only through the command bar;
- no reject-with-a-note;
- allow-always does not say what it allows;
- one question per ask_human, each answer prompting the ant again.
